Package: herdr-core
Architecture: amd64 arm64
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, openssh-client
Recommends: systemd
Description: terminals for coding agents that stay alive
 herdr-core runs programs and coding agents in terminals that keep running
 when the window, the SSH session or the login that started them goes away.
 Start, list, read, attach to, wait on and send keys to terminals from the
 command line or through its JSON-RPC API, locally or on other machines over
 SSH. It is the core the Herdr desktop app (herdr-app) runs its terminals in.
 .
 The command is herdr-core. Upstream calls it hc, but this package does not
 install that alias because httpcode already ships /usr/bin/hc; add
 `alias hc=herdr-core` to your shell if you want it. Under systemd the core
 runs as a user service so it outlives your logins.
